// SR 942.20 — Section 10 Criminal Provisions
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 23 Use of abusive pricing
1 Any person who wilfully:
a. does not implement an ordered price reduction;
b. increases a price despite that being prohibited; or
c. exceeds mutually agreed prices,
shall be liable to a fine not exceeding 100,000 francs.
2 An attempt is a criminal offence.
|

:INFO
Art. 24 Violation of the obligation to provide information
Any person who wilfully:
a. fails to fulfil the duty to provide information (Art. 17); or
b. provides incorrect or incomplete information,
shall be liable to a fine not exceeding 20,000 francs.
|

:INFO
Art. 25 Applicability of administrative criminal law
1 The Administrative Criminal Law Act of 22 March 1974 applies to the prosecution and adjudication of offences.
2 The Federal Department of Economic Affairs, Education and Research is the prosecuting and adjudicating administrative authority.
|

:NOTE
Para. 1 — SR 313.0

